    {
      "annotations": {
        "destructiveHint": false,
        "idempotentHint": true,
        "openWorldHint": true,
        "readOnlyHint": true,
      },
      "description": "A sequence (an ordered series of posts) or one of the site's 5 collections: rationality (Rationality: A-Z, "The Sequences"), codex, hpmor, highlights, bestoflesswrong. sequence = id, URL (/s/<id>, /s/<id>/p/<post>), or a collection slug or URL; sequences have no slugs. For a sequence: title, ids, author, AF status, curated rank, description, the site's word count and reading time (~), and its posts chapter by chapter in the order of the forum's chapter list (the sequence page's own order can differ when chapters are unnumbered), each with ids, title, author, date and karma; limit counts posts. post=<post> (or a /s/<id>/p/<post> URL; giving both with different posts is an error) marks that post: the first page then starts at the chapter containing it and always shows its position with the previous and next posts (call without post to read from the start). At the first or last post of a sequence that belongs to a collection whose books are all numbered, the neighbour is the last or first post of the adjacent sequence in the collection's book order; for bestoflesswrong, whose books are partly unnumbered, the adjacent sequence can't be determined reliably and none is given. If the post is not in this sequence you are told so: a post can be in several sequences, and get_post names only the site's canonical one. For a collection: its description and its books, each with its sequences (open each with get_sequence); limit counts sequences. Books are in number order; where the forum leaves books unnumbered they are listed in the forum's order, which it does not define. af_only keeps only AF posts (or, for a collection, AF sequences), in the same order. Posts that are not publicly visible are left out, as on the site; posts the sequence includes that are reachable by link only are shown, flagged; sequences that are not in the site's sequence lists open by id and are flagged.

